+# Cancellation
+
+For whoever changes cancellation or answers a member who missed the cutoff. Members can cancel a pantry order
+before packing starts, two hours before their pickup slot. Late cancellations left packed bags of fresh food
+unused; a reminder banner had been in the app since summer, but 25 bags were thrown away in October before the
+cutoff was introduced.
+
+## Cutoff
+
+The packing shift starts two hours before each pickup slot. A cancellation before that point costs the pantry
+no packed bag; a later cancellation wastes one. The cutoff therefore follows the start of packing.
+
+Cancellation is allowed strictly before the cutoff and refused at or after it. For a pickup slot starting at
+17:00:
+
+| Cancellation time | Allowed? |
+| --- | --- |
+| Before 15:00 | Yes |
+| Exactly 15:00 | No |
+| After 15:00 | No |
+
+The eligibility check is [`can_cancel(pickup_starts, now)`](../../larder/cancellation.py).
+
+## After the cutoff
+
+A member who cannot come after the cutoff calls the pantry, and the volunteers decide how to handle the request.
+This manual fallback was agreed in [issue 31](../../notes/issue-31.md), together with a request to include the
+pantry's phone number in the refusal message.
+
+## Known limits
+
+The repository contains the eligibility check, but no refusal-message implementation or pantry phone number, so
+the requested phone guidance cannot be verified here. Late requests require manual contact with the pantry;
+obtain its number outside this repository.
